  "id": "COMPOUND:14593 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "Prilocaine, a local anesthetic, is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through its role as a target of multiple isoforms of tyrosine-protein kinase SYK. The evidence suggests that prilocaine may modulate the activity of SYK, which in turn influences the function of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple molecular structures that are targets of SYK and are linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this mechanistic link, suggesting that prilocaine may exert its effects through a pathway involving SYK and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The integration of these findings implies that prilocaine could potentially influence epigenetic processes by interacting with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further experimental validation is required to confirm this mechanism.",
